  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by ${x}^{2}(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+x+1 & =Ax(x+1)+B(x+1)+C{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)^{2}+0+1 & =A(0)(0+1)+B(0+1)+C(0)^{2} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=-1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-1)^{2}+(-1)+1 & =A(-1)(-1+1)+B(-1+1)+C(-1)^{2} \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, letting $x=1$ and using our values for $B$ and $C$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)^{2}+1+1 & =A(1)(1+1)+(1)(1+1)+(3)(1)^{2} \\\\ 5 & =2A+2+3 \\\\ 5 & =2A+5 \\\\ A & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot B\\cdot C=0\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=0.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
